      en: "The Dalat Flower Gardens, formally known as the Dalat City Flower Garden, are a premier botanical attraction in Vietnam's central highlands. Located at the northern tip of Xuan Huong Lake, the gardens span approximately 7,000 square meters and were first established in 1966. After being renovated in 1985, they have become the center of floral diversity in the region, taking advantage of Dalat's cool, temperate mountain climate. The gardens showcase over 300 varieties of flowers, including orchids, hydrangeas, roses, pansies, and mimosas, many of which bloom throughout the year. The landscape features creative topiary, floral arches, and impressive sculptures made entirely of colorful blossoms. A highlights is the extensive orchid house, which protects delicate and rare species from the elements. As the primary venue for the biennial Dalat Flower Festival, the site attracts millions of international and domestic tourists. Beyond their aesthetic appeal, the gardens serve as a major hub for horticultural research and the promotion of the city's thriving flower export industry. The meticulously maintained paths and vibrant displays make it a symbol of Dalat's identity as the flower capital of Vietnam.",
      es: "Los jardines de flores de Đà Lạt (Vườn Hoa Đà Lạt) son el orgullo de la 'ciudad de la eterna primavera' y un centro de esplendor botánico en las tierras altas centrales de Vietnam. Debido a su clima templado, aquí prosperan plantas que apenas sobrevivirían en otras partes del país, incluyendo clásicos europeos y rarezas tropicales. El parque es un destino importante para la cultura de ocio local y el escenario principal del famoso festival anual de las flores, que ha dado a conocer la región mucho más allá de las fronteras nacionales. Geografía K6 — diversidad botánica y clima.",
      pt: "Os jardins de flores de Đà Lạt (Vườn Hoa Đà Lạt) são o orgulho da 'cidade da eterna primavera' e um centro de esplendor botânico no planalto central do Vietname. Devido ao clima ameno, prosperam aqui plantas que dificilmente sobreviveriam noutras partes do país, incluindo clássicos europeus e raridades tropicais. O parque é um destino importante para a cultura de lazer local e o palco principal do famoso festival anual de flores, que tornou a região conhecida muito além das fronteiras nacionais. Geografia K6 — diversidade botânica e clima.",
      fr: "Les jardins de fleurs de Đà Lạt (Vườn Hoa Đà Lạt) sont la fierté de la 'ville de l'éternel printemps' et un centre de splendeur botanique sur les hauts plateaux du centre du Vietnam. Grâce à un climat doux, des plantes qui survivraient difficilement ailleurs au Vietnam s'y épanouissent, des classiques européens aux raretés tropicales. Le parc est une destination majeure de la culture locale et le site principal du célèbre festival annuel des fleurs, qui a fait connaître la région bien au-delà des frontières du pays. Géographie K6 — diversité botanique et climat.",
